We consider a sequence of tasks arriving at user $k$, each of which is characterized by four different features: 
\begin{inparaenum}[(i)]
    % \item task arrival time (in time), denoted by $\taskArrival^k$;
    \item task size/length (in bits),  denoted by $\taskSize^k$;
    % that follows an exponential distribution;
    \item task computational intensity (in CPU cycles per bit), denoted by $\taskIntencity^k$;
