% \textbf{Task Lifetime:}
Upon arrival of each task at the $k^{th}$ user, a decision making agent decides whether the task would be computed on the VR headset or offloaded to the MEC unit for computation using one of the $C$ communication channels. 
We denote $u_k \in \{0, 1, \dots C\}$ as the decision made by the decision making agent regarding the computation location.
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:action}
    u_k := 
    \begin{cases}
         u_k = 0 \;\; \Rightarrow & \text{Compute on VR headset.} \\
        u_k > 0 \;\; \Rightarrow & \text{Offload via channel $u_k$.}
    \end{cases}
\end{equation}
In case of local computation (\ie $u_k = 0$), the task is computed on the local computing unit 
% added to the processing queue
of the $k^{th}$ user.
% for computation.
Alternatively, when the decision-making agent decides to offload the task (\ie $u_k > 0$), the task is transmitted to the MEC unit through
% added to the transmission queue that corresponds to the 
communication channel with index $u_k$.
Then, on the MEC side, the task is computed by the MEC unit, and the computation result is returned to the user through the same communication channel.
% After computing a task, the computation result is added to the transmission queue to be sent back to the corresponding VR headset.
This leads to the following task response time:
% over the $c$'th communication channel (orange path).
% \begin{equation}
%     \taskResponse^k (u_k) = T_a^k + 
%     \begin{cases}
%             u_k = 0 \; &\Rightarrow \taskWaitTime_{1}^k +  \frac{\taskSize^k \taskIntencity^k}{\uavCPUFreq^k}\\
%             u_k > 0 \; &\Rightarrow \taskWaitTime_{2}^{k} + \taskTxTime(S^k, u_k)  
%             + \taskWaitTime_{3} + \frac{\taskSize^k \taskIntencity^k}{\mecCPUFreq^k} \\
%             &+ \;\; \taskWaitTime_{4}^{k} + \resultTxTime(\resultSize^k, u_k) 
%     \end{cases}
% \end{equation}
\begin{equation}
    \taskResponse^k (S^k, I^k, u_k) =
        \begin{cases}
                u_k = 0 \;\; \Rightarrow & \taskExecution(\taskSize^k, \taskIntencity^k, \uavCPUFreq^k).  \\
                u_k > 0 \;\; \Rightarrow & 
                \taskTxTime^k(S^k, u_k) \quad \\
                & \quad + \; \taskExecution(\taskSize^k, \taskIntencity^k, \mecCPUFreq^k) \\
                & \quad + \; \resultTxTime^k(\resultSize^k, u_k).
        \end{cases} \label{eq:tr-const}
\end{equation}
Here, the function $\taskExecution(\taskSize^k, \taskIntencity^k, \uavCPUFreq^k)$ returns the task computation time given the task size $\taskSize^k$, computational intensity $\taskIntencity^k$, and VR headset's CPU frequency $\uavCPUFreq^k$. The function $\taskTxTime(S^k, u_k)$ returns the transmission time and $\resultTxTime(S^k, u_k)$ returns the task result transmission time.
Moreover, 
