\textbf{Communication Model:}
The edge device transmits the task through one of the $C$ available channels to the edge server.
The expected transmission rate for a task is modeled as:
\begin{equation}
    R^k (u_k) = \frac{1}{t_e - t_s} \int_{t_s}^{t_e} R^k_t(u_k) dt,
\end{equation}
where $t_s$ and $t_e$ are the transmission start and end times, respectively, and $R^k_t(u_k)$ is the throughput provided by the uplink communication channel with index $u_k$ for the $k^{th}$ user.
The expected reception rate for a task result is modeled in a similar way over the downlink communication channel. 
% \begin{equation}
%     \underline{R}^k (u_k) = \frac{1}{t_e - t_s} \int_{t_s}^{t_e} \underline{R}^k_t(u_k) dt,
% \end{equation}
