	\subsection{Metrics}
	In our experiment, we evaluated the following indicators. We use Precision and Recall to measure the effectiveness of API classification and API association.
	True Positive(TP) represents the number of correctly classified APIs; The number of API pairs that are correctly associated.
	False Positive (FP) represents the number of APIs classified as P-API (C-API) but not P-API (C-API); The number of API pairs that are judged to be associated with P-APIs and C-APIs but do not exist. False Negative (FN) represents the number of APIs classified as not P-API (C-API) but P-API (C-API); The number of P-API and C-API pairs that are judged not to be associated but are associated. The formulas for  Precision (Pr) and Recall (Re) are as follows.
	\begin{equation}
		Pr = \frac{TP}{TP+FP}, Re = \frac{TP}{TP+FN}
	\end{equation}

