Figure \ref{exp_sim_ann} presents a comparison of hydrogen fractions in the post-reaction mixture as predicted by ANN simulations, theoretical mathematical models, and experimental measurements. The experimental data are represented as blue markers, while green markers correspond to the theoretical simulation results. The predictions made by the ANN closely match both experimental and theoretical data, with a stronger alignment with the experimental data, demonstrating the effectiveness of the network's training. This strong agreement demonstrates the reliability of the ANN in accurately predicting the hydrogen composition in the post-reaction mixture and highlights its potential as a robust tool for modeling complex chemical reaction systems.

