Under an assignment of relative priority points $(\Pi_1, \dots, \Pi_n)$, when a job is added to the ready queue, the new highest-priority job is determined and executed.
Whenever a job finishes or suspends itself, it is removed from the ready queue and a new highest-priority job has to be determined and is executed.

