We let $\Time$ be the domain of the time, which will be either non-negative reals $\setRgeqzero$ (continuous-time semantics) or naturals $\setN$ (discrete-time semantics).
Unless otherwise specified, we assume $\Time = \setRgeqzero$.

\emph{Clocks} are real-valued variables that all evolve over time at the same rate.
Throughout this paper, we assume a set~$\ClockSet = \{ \clocki{1}, \dots, \clocki{\ClockCard} \} $ of \emph{clocks}.
