A \emph{clock valuation} is a function
$\clockval : \ClockSet \rightarrow \Time$, assigning a non-negative value to each clock.
%
We write $\ClocksZero$ for the clock valuation assigning $0$ to all clocks.
Given a constant $d \in \Time$, $\clockval + d$ denotes the valuation \st\ $(\clockval + d)(\clock) = \clockval(\clock) + d$, for all $\clock \in \ClockSet$. If $R$ is a subset of $\ClockSet$ and $\clockval$ a clock valuation, we call \emph{reset} of the clocks of $\resets$ and denote by $[\clockval]_R$ the valuation \st\ for all clock $x \in \ClockSet$, $\reset{\clockval}{\resets}(x) = 0$ if $x \in \resets$ and $\reset{\clockval}{\resets}(x) = \clockval(x)$ otherwise.
