\begin{remark}\label{remark:APub-APriv:AMemo}
By a minor modification on $\APriv$, one can build a TA $\AMemo$ that recognizes exactly the same language as $\TA$ and that stores in each location whether the private locations set has been visited.
To do so, we add the set $\lbrace \locfinal^{\bar{S}} \mid \locfinal \in \FinalSet \rbrace$ to the set of final locations in $\APriv$ and we remove each $\locpriv^{\bar{S}} \in \PrivSet^{\bar{S}}$ from $\LocSet_{\bar{S}}$ in the same way as we did in $\APub$: the private locations of $\AMemo$ are exactly those of $\APriv$.
%
Notably, $\TA$ is weakly (resp.\ fully) opaque if and only if $\AMemo$ is weakly (resp.\ fully) opaque.
\end{remark}
