%The elements of $S$ in separation $(A,B,S)$ are called \emph{portals}.
%Each path in $G$ from $A$ to $B$ must pass through a portal.
Informally, we are interested in separations where $A$ and $B$ have a constant fraction
of the vertices and $S$ is small. 
%uch separations with size depending on the treewidth exist 
Such separations of at most $k$ portals and can be computed efficiently~\cite{BHM20, CABELLO2009815}.
