On the other end, decentralized approaches \citep{egorov2022mamba, liu2024mazero, zhang2024marie} model individual agent dynamics separately and rely on additional mechanisms, such as sophisticated communication or aggregation modules, to recover the global state. However, this misalignment between decentralized model structure and the global Markov decision process (MDP) can impose inherent limitations on model accuracy and those communication or aggregation modules do not have explicit signal for supervision, further hindering the training.
