\subsection{Experiments Setup}\label{sec:exp_setup}
\textbf{Environments.}
We evaluate our method on two widely-used multi-agent continuous control benchmarks requiring heterogeneous-agent cooperation: Multi-Agent MuJoCo (MAMuJoCo) \citep{peng2021facmac} and Bimanual Dexterous Hands (Bi-DexHands) \citep{chen2022bidex}.
MAMuJoCo extends MuJoCo \citep{todorov2012mujoco} to multi-agent settings by partitioning a robot into agents controlling different degrees of freedom (DoFs), requiring coordination for coherent movement. We use seven agent-partitioning settings: HalfCheetah [{2x3}, {3x2}, and {6x1}]; Walker [{2x3} and {3x2}]; and Ant [{2x4} and {4x2}].
Bi-DexHands features dual ShadowRobot hands (26 DoFs each) performing precise bimanual manipulation. We evaluate on four tasks: \emph{ShadowHandPen}, \emph{ShadowHandDoorOpenOutward}, \emph{ShadowHandDoorOpenInward}, and \emph{ShadowHandBottleCap}.
