\subsubsection{New model setup}

The thermal characteristics used are shown in Table \ref{tab:Caracteristiques_thermique}. A soil column of $e_s \ = \ 2 \mathsf{m}$ is considered in the model and a building wall thickness of $e_w \ = \ 4.5 \mathsf{cm}$.  Values of the solar reflectivity (albedo) measured are used for the walls ($0.64$) and for the ground soils ($0.36$). The emissivity is fixed at $0.9$ for each surface (it was not measured). The air volume (dimensions : $ 1.21 \ \times \ 1.68 \ \times \ 1.13 \ \mathsf{m}$ ) has a volumetric heat capacity $c_{air} \ = \ 1.2 \, 10^{\,3} \, \mathsf{J}. \mathsf{m}^{- 3}. \mathsf{K}^{-1}$ The initial temperature is set at $T_0 = 20 \ \mathsf{^\circ C}$ for all the material.
