\begin{lemma}[Infimum and Supremum on $\delta^*$]
    \label{lemma:d}
     Suppose the smallest program size that represents $\rho^*$ is $m^*$, and LGP only uses adding or removing one random instruction as genetic operators to produce offspring. Then an LGP solution with size $m$ has infimum and supremum on $\delta^*_{(m)}$ to access $\rho^*$. Specifically,
    $$\inf{\delta^*_{(m)}}=\max\{0, m^*-m\} \leq \delta^*_{(m)} \leq m^*+m = \sup{\delta^*_{(m)}}.$$
    (For proof refer to Appendix \ref{prf:d})
\end{lemma}

