Let $\rho'_{(o)}$ be the offspring after one of the genetic operators $o\in\mathbb{O}$ is applied to $\rho$ for once, where $\mathbb{O}$ is the set of genetic operators. Let $\Delta \delta^*_{(\rho, o)} = \delta^*(\rho'_{(o)}) - \delta^*(\rho)$ be the difference of $\delta^*$ between $\rho'_{(o)}$ and $\rho$.
