The empirical results confirm that, given a limited range of variation step sizes for freemut, mutating multiple instructions in freemut is better than mutating only one instruction, which is implied by \textbf{Theorem \ref{theo:cons_indi_u}} and its numerical results (Fig. \ref{fig:con_move_N_minigen} and \ref{fig:con_move_N_minigen2}).

