\subsection{Lemma \ref{lemma:UB_con_add}}\label{prf:UB_con_add}
Given an LGP individual $\rho$ whose $\delta^*(\rho)=a+r$ (i.e., accessing $\rho^*$ by adding $a$ necessary instructions and removing $r$ unnecessary instructions), we assume that an operator $o_{+u}$ that adds $u$ instructions into $\rho$ to produce offspring will add any number of unnecessary instructions ($j$) with the same probability. Then, the upper bound of the number of offspring that reduces $\delta^*(\rho)$ by $\Delta \delta^*_{(\rho,o_{+u})}=i$ is \par
